senses.gloss:
1. हस् cl. 1. P. (Dhātup. xvii, 72) हसति (mc. also ˚ते; pf. जहास, जहसे, MBh. &c.; aor. अहसीत् Gr.; fut. हसिता, ib.; हसिष्यति, MBh. &c.; inf. हसितुम्, ib.; ind.p. हसित्वा, -हस्य, ib.),
to laugh, smile, laugh at (instr.), ṢaḍvBr.; Gobh.; MBh. &c.;
to deride, mock, ridicule (acc.), MBh.; R. &c.;
to surpass, excel, Kāvyād.;
to expand, open (as a blossom), Kuval. :
Pass. हस्यते (aor. अहासि), to be laughed or smiled at, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. हासयति (aor. अजीहसत्), to cause to laugh, Hariv.; Kum. :
Desid. जिहसिषति (cf. √ 1. जक्ष्) Gr.:
Intens. जाहस्यते (p. ˚यमान, MBh.), जाहस्ति, to laugh continuously or immoderately, ib.
